  "goodToKnow": "Der Wächter (die Wächterin) is a guard, watchman or guardian: der Nachtwächter (night watchman), der Torwächter (gatekeeper), and figuratively die Wächter der Demokratie. Old towns like Rothenburg ob der Tauber offer evening tours with a costumed Nachtwächter. Wachen means to keep watch; bewachen means to guard; der Wachmann is a security guard. In everyday German, a security guard is usually der Security or der Sicherheitsdienst. Plural: die Wächter."
